#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tuning-other-topics.rst:5
#: 0a134c5162e245dbab32a0e886ba830f
msgid "Additional Tuning Topics"
msgstr "附加调参主题"

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tuning-other-topics.rst:8
#: d0feeaddd24e45d6995199943ed59893
msgid "Tuning ACCEL MAX and Feel"
msgstr "调参 ACCEL MAX 和手感"

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tuning-other-topics.rst:10
#: a65d88c598a4430c99aa9b0f69eda90b
msgid ""
"The final setting for ``ATC_ACCEL_x_MAX`` parameters will depend on the size"
" of the helicopter.  Large 800-900 class machines will typically be in the "
"36000-52000 range; smaller 450-500 class machines will typically be in the "
"90000-110000 range. You may want to experiment with the "
":ref:`ATC_INPUT_TC<ATC_INPUT_TC>` parameter as well to get the initial "
"aircraft response the way you like it.  It is recommended to keep the "
":ref:`ATC_INPUT_TC<ATC_INPUT_TC>` parameter between 0.15 and 0.25.  Once "
"this process is complete, the aircraft should have the desired feel in "
"snappiness and rate."
msgstr ""
"``ATC_ACCEL_x_MAX`` 参数的最终设置取决于直升机的尺寸。大型 800-900 级机器通常在 36000-52000 范围内；较小的 "
"450-500 级机器通常在 90000-110000 范围内。您可能还需要尝试调整 :ref:`ATC_INPUT_TC<ATC_INPUT_TC>`"
" 参数，以获得您喜欢的初始飞行器响应。建议将 :ref:`ATC_INPUT_TC<ATC_INPUT_TC>` 参数保持在 0.15 到 0.25 "
"之间。此过程完成后，飞行器应具有期望的操控灵敏度和速率感。"

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tuning-other-topics.rst:18
#: 05ed80e4c1af4345a9d859914d1dc833
msgid ""
"Below is a graph showing an example of Rate Roll Desired vs actual Rate "
"Roll. The peak corresponds to a rapid stick input and the amplitude (height)"
" of the peaks should be approximately the same with no more than 100 "
"milliseconds offset."
msgstr "以下图表显示了速率横滚期望值与实际速率横滚的示例。峰值对应快速摇杆输入，峰值的幅度（高度）应大致相同，偏移不超过 100 毫秒。"

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tuning-other-topics.rst:27
#: 0523c813596c482797a7abf768e0ed76
msgid "Setting IMAX and ILMI"
msgstr "设置 IMAX 和 ILMI"

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tuning-other-topics.rst:28
#: 585038ba53e043d38fbf32186514d902
msgid ""
"The IMAX value limits amount of integrator error that can be stored to "
"counter large disturbances in attitude.  In the pitch axis this is set by "
"the integrator error required to hold the aircraft attitude at high forward "
"speeds.  The starting value is 0.4.  To check this set the value to IMAX = "
"1, fly the aircraft at the maximum desired speed.  Pull the log and look at "
"what the maximum I value is in the PIDP message.  Set IMAX for 0.1 above the"
" maximum value.  You could do the same for the roll axis but typically 0.4 "
"should be sufficient.  ILMI is set for the maximum amount of integrator that"
" you want to retain in a hover to help maintain attitude.  It is recommended"
" that this value is no larger than 0.1"
msgstr ""
"IMAX 值限制可存储以抵抗大姿态扰动的积分误差量。在俯仰轴上，这由以高前飞速度保持飞行器姿态所需的积分误差设定。起始值为 0.4。要检查此值，将 "
"IMAX 设为 1，以最大期望速度飞行飞行器。调取日志并查看 PIDP 消息中的最大 I 值。将 IMAX 设为最大值加 "
"0.1。横滚轴可以做同样的操作，但通常 0.4 应该足够。ILMI 设置为您希望在悬停中保留的最大积分量，以帮助保持姿态。建议此值不超过 0.1"

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tuning-other-topics.rst:38
#: 1c039411a7fb4adeac1cb3e76eed6a49
msgid ""
"Below is a graph of desired roll attitude vs actual roll attitude for a "
"helicopter in high-speed autonomous flight with the ILMI parameters set to "
"zero. The effect of the I-gain and IMAX parameters, properly set, will make "
"the helicopter track the desired attitude very closely at speed exceeding "
"5m/s for more than 2 seconds (what we call “dynamic flight”). It should be "
"within 1-2 degrees of desired in dynamic flight. Towards the right side of "
"the graph the helicopter came to a stop in hover and the pilot switched to "
"Stabilize flight mode. You will notice a discrepancy between the actual and "
"desired roll attitude at that point. This is the effect of having ILMI set "
"to zero. The ILMI can be considered to be a sort of “auto trim” for hover "
"that will reduce the discrepancy between desired and actual pitch and roll "
"attitude when the helicopter is not in dynamic flight."
msgstr ""
"以下是一架直升机在高速自主飞行时，ILMI 参数设为零情况下期望横滚姿态与实际横滚姿态的图表。I 增益和 IMAX 参数正确设置后，直升机在超过 "
"5m/s 持续 2 秒以上的速度（我们称之为\"动态飞行\"）下跟踪期望姿态的效果会非常好，应在动态飞行中偏差在 1-2 "
"度以内。在图表右侧，直升机在悬停中停止，飞手切换到 Stabilize 飞行模式。您会注意到此时实际横滚姿态和期望横滚姿态之间有差异。这是 ILMI "
"设为零的效果。ILMI 可以视为悬停的一种\"自动配平\"，当直升机不在动态飞行时，它将减少期望俯仰和横滚姿态与实际姿态之间的差异。"

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tuning-other-topics.rst:55
#: 5c656ee4956a45f3b3a78f4857792ca8
msgid "Adjusting I-gains For High-Speed Autonomous Flight"
msgstr "为高速自主飞行调整 I 增益"

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tuning-other-topics.rst:57
#: 98490530622442139ad6029606f56e94
msgid ""
"Prepare a mission with your ground station software that will fly the "
"helicopter, preferably in a figure-8 pattern to make both right and left "
"turns, at a speed of 6 m/s. Fly the helicopter on this mission, pull the "
"logs from the microSD card and look at the AHRS desired vs actual pitch, "
"roll and yaw attitudes in dynamic flight. They should track within 1-2 "
"degrees. If they do not, increase the ``ATC_RAT_xxx_I`` value for that axis "
"until they do."
msgstr ""
"用您的地面站软件准备一个任务，以 6 m/s 的速度飞行直升机，最好采用 8 字形模式以进行左右转弯。在此任务上飞行直升机，从 microSD "
"卡调取日志，查看动态飞行中 AHRS 期望俯仰、横滚和偏航姿态与实际姿态的对比。它们应在 1-2 度以内跟踪。如果没有，增加该轴的 "
"``ATC_RAT_xxx_I`` 值，直到满足要求。"

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tuning-other-topics.rst:64
#: f4fb5542a29647eda3981d4d821e665a
msgid ""
"Now, fly the same mission, but at higher speed of 9-10 m/s, and analyze the "
"logs the same way. Make further adjustments to the I-gains and IMAX values "
"as required. It is not clear what I-gain values will be required as no two "
"helicopters are the same. But I-gain values from 0.25 - 0.38 are common in "
"pitch and roll, and 0.18 - 0.30 in yaw. IMAX values of 0.40 - 0.45 are "
"common, however refer to the 'Setting IMAX, and ILMI' section on how to "
"determine what the IMAX value should be."
msgstr ""
"现在以更高速度 9-10 m/s 飞行相同任务，并以相同方式分析日志。根据需要进一步调整 I 增益和 IMAX 值。不清楚需要什么样的 I "
"增益值，因为没有两架直升机完全相同。但俯仰和横滚的 I 增益值在 0.25-0.38 范围内常见，偏航在 0.18-0.30 范围内常见。IMAX 值在"
" 0.40-0.45 范围内常见，但请参阅\"设置 IMAX 和 ILMI\"部分了解如何确定 IMAX 值。"

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tuning-other-topics.rst:73
#: ec704cb389834744a19a973d2327968b
msgid "Preventing I term Build Up"
msgstr "防止 I 项积累"

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tuning-other-topics.rst:75
#: 01cc6beaa8314467b0c30391e31e9723
msgid ""
"A downside of the I term is that it can build if the vehicle is constrained "
"in its movement, so as not to be able to respond and reduce any long term "
"errors, as when still on the ground. The I term can build to its maximum "
"value and could possibly tip over the vehicle. Two methods are provided to "
"avoid this."
msgstr ""
"I 项的缺点是，当飞行器受到运动约束而无法响应和减少任何长期误差时（如仍在地面上时），I 项可能积累。I "
"项可能积累到最大值，可能导致飞行器翻倒。提供了两种方法来避免这种情况。"

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tuning-other-topics.rst:77
#: 7a41ec8771ea49eb882c0a15263ef466
msgid ""
"The first is by restricting by providing a \"leak\" mechanism (constantly "
"reduced at a specified rate) when on the ground or hover(actually when "
"moving with a GPS speed of less than 5m/s). To prevent the I term from "
"completely disappearing at low speeds or hover, the parameters "
":ref:`ATC_RAT_RLL_ILMI<ATC_RAT_RLL_ILMI>` and :ref:`ATC_RAT_PIT_ILMI "
"<ATC_RAT_PIT_ILMI>`, only lets it leak off so much. So the integrator leak "
"along with the leak minimum parameter keep enough of the integrator to make "
"it effective in keeping the attitudes matching but not so powerful to cause "
"the aircraft to roll over."
msgstr ""
"第一种方法是通过在地面或悬停时（实际上是当GPS速度低于5m/s时移动）提供\"泄漏\"机制（以指定速率持续减少）来限制I项。为了防止I项在低速或悬停时完全消失，参数"
" :ref:`ATC_RAT_RLL_ILMI<ATC_RAT_RLL_ILMI>` 和 :ref:`ATC_RAT_PIT_ILMI "
"<ATC_RAT_PIT_ILMI>` "
"仅允许其泄漏到一定程度。因此，积分器泄漏加上泄漏最小参数可以保留足够的积分器，使其有效地保持姿态匹配，但又不至于太强而导致飞机翻滚。"

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tuning-other-topics.rst:81
#: a6edf54293a14fcbb98ba607d7d82648
msgid ""
"The second is to use ArduPilot's landing and takeoff detection algorithms to"
" zero the I terms when on the ground, and allow it to operate normally after"
" takeoff."
msgstr "第二种方法是使用 ArduPilot 的降落和起飞检测算法，在地面时将I项归零，并在起飞后允许其正常运行。"

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tuning-other-topics.rst:83
#: 8be4d2e854ed49a981253dd7af7d9882
msgid ""
"Which method is used is determined by the :ref:`H_OPTIONS<H_OPTIONS>` "
"bitmask. Setting bit 0 (ie \"1\" for the parameter value) will use the first"
" method with a leaky integrator.It is the default method. But clearing that "
"bit (value = \"0\"), will use the second method, which is now usually "
"preferred."
msgstr ""
"使用哪种方法由 :ref:`H_OPTIONS<H_OPTIONS>` "
"位掩码决定。将第0位设置为（即参数值为\"1\"）将使用带泄漏积分器的第一种方法，这是默认方法。但清除该位（值为\"0\"）将使用第二种方法，这种方法现在通常更受青睐。"
